<title>INDIA: India soybean, oil, meal steady in dull volumes.</title>
<headline>India soybean, oil, meal steady in dull volumes.</headline>
<dateline>INDORE, India 1997-02-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Soybean prices remained steady in central Indian markets and plant delivery condition, dealers said on Monday.</p>
<p>Arrivals were around 2,500 tonnes in central Indian markets. Business volumes were dull and the undertone was steady.</p>
<p>Soyoil prices were steady in very limited trading. Business volume was dull and the undertone was steady.</p>
<p>Soymeal and rapeseed extraction prices were steady. Soymeal yellow was $283-284 per tonne in export. Rapeseed extraction was $116 for ready shipment and was $109-110 for March shipment in export. Rapeseed extraction was 3,900 rupees for ready delivery, 3,800 rupees for March delivery and was 3,700 rupees per tonne for April delivery in  FOR (Free on Rail) condition. Business volume was extremely low and the undertone was steady.</p>
